---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const BASE = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Work"
  description="Engagement shapes if you want me on the problem."
  lede="If you want me on the problem, here are the shapes that work. Each one has a clear goal, a fixed window, and a written hand-off."
  nav="work"
>
  <section class="prose">
    <h2>Engagement shapes</h2>

    <h3>Diagnostic — 2 weeks</h3>
    <p>
      I land, read the org, talk to the people who own the platform decisions, and ship a written
      diagnosis. Specific risks, named owners, ranked fixes. You decide what to act on.
    </p>
    <p><strong>Good fit:</strong> "We can feel something is off but cannot name it." Outputs: 1 written report, 1 leadership read-out, 0 pull requests.</p>

    <h3>Operating-model rewrite — 6 to 12 weeks</h3>
    <p>
      Define the ownership matrix, the platform contracts, the cadence, the meeting set, the on-call
      shape. Drive adoption with the leadership team. Leave behind written agreements, not slides.
    </p>
    <p><strong>Good fit:</strong> The platform team is overworked, product teams are blocked, and you've already tried the obvious reorg.</p>

    <h3>Embedded R&D ops — 3 to 6 months, part-time</h3>
    <p>
      I work alongside your VP/CTO on the connective tissue. Quarterly planning, hiring posture,
      platform debt prioritisation, vendor decisions, exec read-outs. Senior-engineer-shaped, not
      consultant-shaped.
    </p>
    <p><strong>Good fit:</strong> You have the bench but the cadence is not holding.</p>

    <h2>How to start</h2>
    <p>
      <a href={`${BASE}contact`}>Send a one-paragraph brief</a>: what is happening, what you have tried,
      what you want to be true in 90 days. I reply within a week. First call is free; we use it to
      decide whether the engagement shape fits.
    </p>

    <h2>What I will not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Audit reports without a written remediation plan.</li>
      <li>Long retainers without a stop condition.</li>
      <li>Replace your VP/CTO. I work for them, not around them.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
